Package: easyPR
Title: Prognostic Meta-Analysis, Made Teachable
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Vanio", "Antunes", email = "vanio.antunes.md@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A front end for the meta-analysis of a prognostic model's
    performance, argued like the 'meta' package. One call takes a table of
    external validations and a measure, either "cstat" for discrimination or
    "OE" for calibration, works out each study's estimate and standard error
    from whatever it reported, pools them, and returns the pooled performance
    with its heterogeneity and prediction interval. Companion plots cover a
    forest of the validations, leave-one-out, meta-regression on study-level
    covariates with a bubble plot, and a funnel with a test of asymmetry.
    Estimation is delegated to 'metamisc'. Built alongside the free book at
    <https://vanioljantunes.github.io/easyPR/>.
